# Line endings for Markdown. The repo runs with core.autocrlf=true, so .md files
# land on disk as CRLF while every blob in HEAD is already LF (measured
# 2026-11-23: 266 tracked .md, 0 with CRLF in the blob, 143 with CRLF on disk).
# Pinning text eol=lf makes checkout and index normalisation agree, so a .md diff
# shows content and never a whole-file rewrite.
*.md text eol=lf

# Override -- one file, and it is the exception the broad rule above would misjudge.
# .council/rule_guardrail_solar_rag/round1/RAG_SOLAR_SYSTEM_RULE_MAP.md holds
# 40,594 NUL bytes in 81,420 B (measured 2026-11-23, byte-identical in HEAD blob
# and on disk), which is why git auto-classified it binary before any attributes
# file existed. "*.md text" forces it back to text: inert on TODAY's bytes
# (git hash-object with the attribute and with none agree --
# ee346a19c452a4fd0bb8683acbd8aa4c307f02f9), but a text diff/apply path over NUL
# content is exactly how a later edit gets mangled. Pin it to binary again.
.council/rule_guardrail_solar_rag/round1/RAG_SOLAR_SYSTEM_RULE_MAP.md -text
